    "result": "The frai-core suite now passes: 28 of 28 tests. There were two separate bugs, both in source, and I didn't touch any test files.\n\n- **Governance (`finetune/index.js`):** `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was only reachable through the default export, but the test imports it by name. I added a named re-export.\n- **Eval (`eval/metrics.js`):** `runEvaluations` calls every metric as `(outputs, references)`. `toxicityMetric`'s second parameter is the list of banned terms, so it was treating the reference strings as banned words. \"friendly world\" then matched the reference \"friendly world\" and scored 0 instead of 1. `DEFAULT_METRICS` now uses a small wrapper that passes only the outputs to `toxicityMetric`. `toxicityMetric` itself and its exports are unchanged.",
